{
  "abstract": "Over half of known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. Parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$ makes the regular fifths linear in $S_{ab}$ and completes the square in all three remaining conditions, cutting out the Branch-1 and twin-fifth sextuple surfaces. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and the first rational almost septuple of relation type $(5,2)$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness on $H$ by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. Varying the base quadruple via algebraic syzygies yields the universal osculating $18/21$ surface over $w_1(q)=(q^2-3)/(2q)$, the dual $(X_1,X_2)$-secant $18/21$ surfaces $R(K,\\Lambda)$ and $R_{22}(\\tilde{K},\\tilde{\\Lambda})$ supporting eight $19/21$ families across the four outer-gate branches ($4$ genus-zero and $4$ elliptic) and two reciprocal genus-zero $19/21$ conics on the $1+u_0c^*_-=\\square$ double cover, the universal $\\varphi_g$-reflected cross-chord, norm-coupling, and Euler-Chasles calculus on tangent triples ($17/21$ step-$1$, step-$2$, step-$3$, and two-shift ladders over $\\mathcal{T}_{\\mathrm{tan}}(s)$ and the $S_3\\times(\\mathbb{Z}/2\\mathbb{Z})$-symmetric surface $W^2=2(x^2+y^2)(x^2+z^2)(y^2+z^2)$, plus $19/21$ $4$-torsion orbit ladders on $v^2=h^2\\pm h$), and the QRT Vieta-jumping tower $Q_{n-1}=[n]P_\\infty\\oplus T_0$ on $E_W(R^2,Z)$. On the outer-gate branches, the unpaid gates descend to $Z=w_1^2$ as irreducible degree-$20$ curves of genus $g_Z=9$, finite by Faltings' theorem; along the canonical section $Z=8(R+1)$, $n=1$ is the unique degenerate level, every $n\\ge 2$ gives non-degenerate $\\ge 18/21$ families with quadratic degree growth governed by $\\hat{h}(P_\\infty)=1/2$, and for $n\\in\\{2,3,4,5\\}$ each unpaid gate has genus $g\\ge 5$. No rational septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 42 (Adds Theorem 20(147)-(149) and exp97-exp99 to Section 9(c.1), THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, and verify_paper.py; updates 94-file supplement.zip at 565,023 bytes compressed and 1,884,136 bytes uncompressed < 2,000,000 bytes): (1) Theorem 20(147) (exp97): Establishes the universal dimensionless (D,S,rho_mp) dictionary for tangent triples, the explicit factorization P_{12,mp} = F_{6,mp}^{(-)} F_{6,mp}^{(+)} over Q[g,h,v] governing the step-2 self-reflection gate 1 + u_{2,mp}*phi_g(u_{2,mp}) = -P_{self,mp}*F_{6,mp}^{(-)}*F_{6,mp}^{(+)}/(A_mp^2 B_mp^2), the three-term norm coupling N_g(d_{eps_1}, u_{2,eps_2}), the universal moduli inverse map and Pythagorean Cosine Law 1 - alpha*beta = S^2 = (1 - alpha*m)^2 on S_sym: W^2 = 2(x^2+y^2)(x^2+z^2)(y^2+z^2), and the quadratic splitting of the 4-torsion loci v^2 = h^2 +- h on S_sym; (2) Theorem 20(148) (exp98): Proves the Universal Spoke-Root Addition, Trace, Norm, and Reflection-Defect Product Law g*U(Q)^2*R_mp^2*(phi_g(x_mp) - x_pm) = R_{1,mp}^2*R^2*(phi_g(d_mp) - d_pm)*(phi_g(x) - x) for every Q in (P_0 + 2E_Y(Q)) cap E_Y(Q), deduces fixed-point-freeness of Phi_g on the rational coset via Fermat's right-triangle theorem (y^2 = x^4 - 1 has no rational points with y != 0), and establishes 3-Step Cayley Reciprocity and universal 17/21 step-3 ladders S_{7,mp}^{step3}; (3) Theorem 20(149) (exp99): Establishes the Universal Self-Reflection Annulus Law, 2x2 Spoke-Root Cramer System, Symmetric Euler-Chasles Correspondence B(R,X) = 0 on P_0 + 2E_Y(Q), Dual Norm Square-Completions of N_g(x,x_mp), explicit two-shift step-3 rungs u_{3,2mp} = x([3]P_0 mp [2]S_Y) with telescoping self-reflection factorization g^2*N_{3,mp}^2*D_{3,mp}^2*(1 + u_{3,mp}*phi_g(u_{3,mp})) = P_{4,mp}^{(3)}*P_{8,mp}^{(3)}, 4-torsion norm unification P_{4,-}^{(3)}*P_{4,+}^{(3)} = -P_{6,pm}(h) mod (v^2 - (h^2 +- h)), and universal 17/21 two-shift step-3 ladders S_{7,mp}^{(3,1-2)}.",
